              "text": "The latest iPhone models belong to the **iPhone 17 series** (including the standard **iPhone 17**, the ultra-thin **iPhone Air**, the **iPhone 17 Pro**, and the premium **iPhone 17 Pro Max**) as well as the budget-friendly **iPhone 17e**. \n\nWhere you can buy them depends on your preference for buying unlocked (outright) or on a carrier contract, as well as your geographic location. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Directly from Apple (Best for buying unlocked & trade-ins)\nBuying straight from Apple is the most reliable way to get a brand-new, fully unlocked iPhone.\n* **Online:** You can purchase via the official [Apple Store website](https://www.apple.com) or the Apple Store app.\n* **Physical Stores:** Visit any physical Apple Retail Store to see the colors and sizes in person.\n* **Benefits:** \n  * **Apple Trade-In:** You can trade in your old iPhone for instant credit toward your new one.\n  * **Financing:** Apple offers 0% interest financing options through Apple Card Monthly Installments (US) or partner banks globally.\n  * **AppleCare+:** Easy to add accidental damage protection during checkout.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Major Mobile Carriers (Best for contract deals & bill credits)\nIf you don't mind staying on a contract, major wireless carriers offer aggressive promotions. You can often get the latest iPhone heavily discounted\u2014or even \"free\"\u2014via monthly bill credits when trading in an old device or adding a new line.\n\n* **United States:** Verizon, AT&T, T-Mobile, and Boost Mobile.\n* **United Kingdom:** Three, Vodafone, EE, and O2.\n* **Romania / Europe:** Orange, Vodafone, and Digi.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Major Electronics Retailers (Best for rewards points & upfront sales)\nYou can buy the iPhone outright or set up carrier financing directly through giant retail chains, which frequently offer store-specific gift cards or reward points with a purchase.\n\n* **United States:** Best Buy, Target, Walmart, and Costco. \n* **United Kingdom:** Currys, Argos, and Amazon UK.\n* **Romania:** \n  * **iSTYLE:** As the official Apple Premium Reseller, they provide the exact same stock and official warranty as an Apple Store.\n  * **eMAG & Altex:** Major local retailers that frequently offer fast shipping, seasonal promotions, and interest-free installment plans.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Certified Refurbished and Second-Hand (Best for saving money)\nIf you want the latest generation but want to save some cash, look for open-box or lightly used models:\n* **Flip.ro / Rejoy:** Outstanding local options in Eastern Europe (Romania, Bulgaria, Greece, Hungary) for buying thoroughly tested, certified refurbished iPhone 17 models with a warranty.\n* **Back Market:** A reliable global marketplace for refurbished tech.\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 Tips Before You Buy:\n* **Check for Carrier Deals:** If you have been with your carrier for a long time, look at their \"loyalty upgrades\". Many of them match the trade-in values offered to new customers.\n* **Storage Matters:** Note that the base iPhone 17 models start at **256GB** of storage\u2014giving you double the starting space of older generations without an increase in base price.",
